# Quotes of docs/guide/troubleshooting.md that tools/check/troubleshooting-msgs.sh cannot match to one string of the
# source (one text per line, exactly as quoted); the reason is on the line above each group.
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:88 appends "set -D$WORKDIR", a constant holding the property name.
…; if the work directory is mounted noexec set -Dkuicksilver.native.workdir
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:183-195 builds "work directory <dir> " + one of several refusals ("is a symbolic link", "is not a
# directory", "is owned by <owner>, not by this user", ...) + "; set -D$WORKDIR to a directory only you own".
work directory <dir> is a symbolic link / is not a directory / is owned by <owner>, not by this user / keeps group/other permissions …; set -Dkuicksilver.native.workdir to a directory only you own
# KslLoader.jvm.kt:107 passes "OpenSSL 3.5+ (not 4.x)" as the required version of KslException.Version("OpenSSL <found> found, ... required").
OpenSSL <found> found, OpenSSL 3.5+ (not 4.x) required
# Http3Endpoint.kt:122 interpolates the constant: "the server chose ALPN \"$alpn\", not \"$H3\"".
the server chose ALPN \"<alpn>\", not \"h3\"
